803:**Phase 6 — Code review.** Each non-implementer commits their `review/round-NN/<agent-id>.md`. No native review surface — discussion lives in the review files.
805:**Phase 7 — Review consensus.** Drafter commits `review/consensus.md`; signoffs appended in follow-up commits.
807:**Phase 8 — Fix-up.** Implementer pushes fix-up commits to `feature/<slug>` (in code repo), then updates `IMPLEMENTATION.md` (in parley-deck) with the fix-up cycle section and a new commit `[<agent>] <slug>: IMPLEMENTATION.md fix-up cycle N — ready for re-review`. When complete, status flips to `complete` in a final commit `[<agent>] <slug>: IMPLEMENTATION.md — complete`. The code-repo branch may or may not be merged — that is the code repo's own concern, not this protocol's.
817:- **Design PR** in the parley-deck repo — covers Phases 0–4. Branch: `idea/<slug>`. Title: `[<slug>] design`. Merged at Phase 4 close.
818:- **Implementation PR** in the code repo — covers Phases 5–8. Branch: `feature/<slug>`. Title: `[<slug>] implementation`. Merged when Phase 8 reaches `status: complete`.
822:**Files are canonical, PR is ergonomic.** Every artifact lives as a file in `ideas/<slug>/`. The PR exposes those files via the **Files changed** tab to humans, and the PR's **Conversation** tab is the natural surface for chat-like cross-review and clarifications. Substantive positions still go into the round files; PR comments are non-authoritative.
