   172	### Phase 0.0 — Track selection (conditional rigor)
   173	
   174	Not every change needs the full lifecycle. Each idea runs on one of three **tracks**, set as
   175	`track: fast | standard | deliberation` in `00-prompt.md` (default `standard`). The track is a
   176	**mechanical routing decision** from the classifier below — it scales ceremony to risk. Round
   177	content (analysis, review, refutation) is always model-driven; only the routing is objective.
   178	
   179	**Classifier — check the `deliberation` triggers first; first match wins:**
   180	
   181	| → `deliberation` if ANY                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              | → `fast` if ALL                                                                                              | → `standard` (default)                                              |
   182	| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |
   183	| protocol change (§7); security / auth / secrets / payments / privacy / production infra; data migration / irreversible / destructive op; `strict_gate: true`; `auto_implement`; pipeline or action block (§12); public-API or persisted-schema break; > ~15 files / ~1000 LOC | fully reversible; ≤ ~3–5 files / ~300 LOC; no security or data surface; mechanically verifiable (lint / type / test) | everything that is neither forced to `deliberation` nor fully `fast` |
   184	
   185	**Per-track behavior** (the invariants below hold on every track):
   186	
   187	| Aspect                        | `fast`                                     | `standard` (default)                        | `deliberation`                          |
   188	| ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- |
   189	| §9.0 readiness ping           | skipped                                     | full                                        | full                                    |
   190	| Cross-review rounds (Phase 2) | skipped                                     | capped at 2, then escalate/upgrade          | unbounded                               |
   191	| Consensus + FINAL (Phase 3–4) | collapsed: one `FINAL.md` with embedded signoffs | separate, drafted simultaneously        | separate                                |
   192	| Reviewers (Phase 6)           | 1 (model-diverse)                           | 2                                           | all non-implementers                    |
   193	| Fix-up (Phase 8)              | cap 1 cycle; fix-only verification ok       | cap 2 cycles; fix-only verify for narrow fixes | unbounded; `strict_gate` available   |
   194	| Timeout per agent             | ~5 min                                      | ~15 min                                     | ~30 min                                 |
   195	| Auto-advance                  | full (pause only for the one signoff)       | auto-advance; human gate at FINAL→implementation | human gate at each transition      |
   196	
   197	**Invariants on every track (never dropped for speed):** at least one independent
   198	non-facilitator artifact (non-solo, §1); refutation-default review — the reviewer *count*
   199	shrinks by track, the refutation discipline never does; round-1 independence (Phase 1);
   200	append-only ✅/🟡/❌ signoffs; files-canonical audit trail; the §14 human brake; English-only;
   201	no-secrets. (Rules tagged `LE-N` below are the loop-engineering rules; the tag is only a
   202	reference id — the rule text is what binds.)
   203	
   204	**Binding, challenge & mid-idea upgrade.** The track is binding once Phase 0 closes, but any
   205	participant may **force-upgrade** to a stricter track — an `inbox/` note before round-1 closes,

